{"repository": "sveltejs/svelte", "task_candidate_id": 24416, "repository_id": 283, "issue_number": 18934, "github_issue_id": 5725524244, "html_url": "https://github.com/sveltejs/svelte/issues/18934", "created_at": "2026-10-06T08:40:02+00:00", "author_association": null, "title": "`&` in a constant `class` becomes `&amp;` on the client when the element has scoped styles", "body_text": "### Describe the bug

When an element is scoped by the component's `<style>` and the client compiler passes a constant `class` string to `$.set_class`, it HTML-escapes that string first. `set_class` assigns the string to `className` (or calls `setAttribute`), and neither decodes entities, so `&`, `<` and `"` reach the DOM as `&amp;`, `&lt;` and `&quot;`.

```svelte
<script>
	const variant = '[&>*]:a';
</script>

<span class="b {variant}">span</span>

<style>
	.b {
		color: red;
	}
</style>
```

Client output (5.57.1, `dev: false`):

```js
$.set_class(span, 1, 'b [&amp;>*]:a svelte-n50uah');
```

The server output is correct, since the browser decodes the entity when it parses the HTML:

```js
$$renderer.push(`<span class="b [&amp;>*]:a svelte-n50uah">span</span>`);
```

So with SSR, the element starts with the class `b [&>*]:a svelte-n50uah`. During hydration, `set_class` sees that its value differs from the server attribute and writes `b [&amp;>*]:a svelte-n50uah`. Without SSR, the class is wrong from the start. In our app this broke Tailwind arbitrary variants such as `[&>*:first-child]:shrink-0` after hydration, and the result was a layout shift.

The value has to compile to a string literal that goes to `set_class`. I found four ways that happens:

- an interpolation whose values the compiler can evaluate: a `const` string, a `let` or `$state` that is never reassigned, a module-level `const`, or an inline string (`class="b {'[&>*]:a'}"`);
- a string literal written as an expression: `class={'b [&>*]:a'}`;
- static class text on an element that also has a `class:` directive;
- static class text on a custom element, or on a `<svelte:element>` with no other attributes and no `style:` directives.

The escaping arrived in 5.20.3 (#15352). Interpolated `const` and `let` values have reached it since 5.27.0, when partial evaluation was added (#15494).

These are not affected:

- elements without scoped styles, because no hash is appended and the literal is passed unescaped;
- static class text on a regular element without `class:` directives, which is written into the template markup;
- elements with spread attributes, and `<svelte:element>` with other attributes or `style:` directives, which use `attribute_effect` with the raw value;
- a single expression that isn't a string literal, such as `class={X}` or ``class={`b ${X}`}``, because it isn't folded;
- other attributes (`title`, `data-*`, `style`), whose folded values are passed to `set_attribute` / `set_style` unescaped.

The cause is `build_set_class` in `packages/svelte/src/compiler/phases/3-transform/client/visitors/shared/element.js`, added in #15352:

```js
value = b.literal(escape_html(value.value, true) + ' ' + context.state.analysis.css.hash);
```

Escaping is right for values written into template markup, but this literal only ever goes to `set_class`. I intend to submit a PR that removes the `escape_html` call.

### Reproduction

[Playground](https://svelte.dev/playground/untitled#H4sIAAAAAAAAE22P0U7DMAxFf8WyEANUte9Zmokf4AeWPaSpJyJlaVSbwVTl31GiAS-8xMq51_b1hsldCBX66JiB2LtMM3Z4DpEY1XFDueVqqAC7H_trzj1fKUplk2P6j_slCSVhVKjZryGLscmKXxILXN0aXBIYYXd8NC8n5Xb7qkYS4OwSjPDA4oSenvc26eFvQNJNn0KalbwHHrf6L9BOGC1OsN2HF4umanqor7FJZ9Ncb-5CCrRfZjKt-9D_8qKHxvWQ79vkFqkl7yfYaq03xGVVsNLcQpeW8O7DDoW-BJWsH1ROHYoL8TOkGdXZRabyDZ0XDml1AQAA). It renders `className: b [&amp;>*]:a svelte-n50uah`, and the compiled JS passes the escaped literal to `$.set_class`.

