### Describe the bug

An effect teardown reads a $derived, in the same flush that replaced the nested state the derived reads. Since 5.35.5, the derived then stops tracking that nested state. A later in-place change to the new nested object never reaches the derived or anything that reads it.

My reading of the cause: #16278 re-evaluates a derived read during teardown against the values from before the change. That run also records the derived's dependencies, so the derived ends up depending on the old nested objects instead of the new ones. #16363 had the same cause. Its fix, #16438, skips the re-run only for a derived with no dependencies, which does not cover this case.

Bisected over published releases: 5.35.4 passes and 5.35.5 fails. 5.57.2 still fails.



### Reproduction

repro.svelte.js:
```
import { flushSync } from 'svelte';

export function run(teardownReads) {
	const state = $state({ items: [] });
	const derived = $derived(state.items.map((item) => item.done));
	const seen = [];
	const dispose = $effect.root(() => {
		$effect(() => {
			seen.push(derived.join(','));
		});
		$effect(() => {
			if (derived.length === 0) {
				$effect(() => () => {
					if (teardownReads) void derived.length;
				});
			}
		});
	});
	flushSync();
	state.items = [{ done: false }]; // replace the nested array
	flushSync();
	state.items[0].done = true; // change it in place
	flushSync();
	dispose();
	return seen;
}
```
App.svelte:

```
<script>
	import { run } from './repro.svelte.js';

	let result = $state('');
</script>

<button onclick={() => (result = JSON.stringify({ control: run(false), teardownRead: run(true) }))}>
	run
</button>
<pre>{result}</pre>
```
Expected, and what 5.35.4 gives:
```
control:      ["", "false", "true"]
teardownRead: ["", "false", "true"]
```
5.35.5 to 5.57.2 give:
```
control:      ["", "false", "true"]
teardownRead: ["", "false"]
```

The only difference between the two runs is the derived.length read in the teardown. The teardown runs when the inner effect is destroyed, in the flush where state.items is replaced.

Playground, failing on 5.57.2: https://svelte.dev/playground/hello-world?version=5.57.2#H4sIAAAAAAAAE4WSTW_bMAyG_wohDLAEGE7PThxgt2GHDViPcQ6uTTfqFMqQ6KSB4f8-SHY-22InSyRf8uVjDYKqPYpc_EBjLBytMw1IbDRjo0QqWm3Qi3wzCD51oS4ERHpWfe-6zB_QcIi9VB4_i9eWGIm9yMXK1053vC6pZL3vrGMYwPUEI7TO7iHJFg47Z2dx9uaTZUmh2iCDQ98bhgK-ea4YZZKoZUmrxbUprV56ZktgqTa6_lsMUkGxBnmR_nz-_Svz7DS96vYkBwjunDV5sCHbynhUKTBWrrFH-oNVM2XY9ahgVGqM5l0fhi2maeuSVp3D9TBNGVeLcBOpYHxnkQfpmH5B8GHde4wfkzcsL_xa0_vd84nqC8VJEdDheyxqe6pZW5pWuVnOKxjCPrUlzxCxXvkOoBn3PofNFsaA-lzXoNMHbELlfJRRkcX6bF91UoZjZB8OWWMJ1W0Lj0hQwGZ721b7zvpoANsWa86ctSynXxhtljxnzsHYJ-t6v5Ozk-zNapJJmii1PLv-IJuCJesWLjqD9Mo7KIoCntS15FF7HhykDyQPVjdw3-7GQsnjdJgj8-fy9-R0vwEZ-AwQ0OUQXyaM2_9pNk_bCBsKCO_u0_KZ83xzyL2jCHJZ0ljS_cPdpoIrbY6aGpFHF6mo_InqOf8Pe4JuQEIEAAA

The same code passing on 5.35.4: https://svelte.dev/playground/hello-world?version=5.35.4#H4sIAAAAAAAAE4WSTW_bMAyG_wohDLAEGE7PThxgt2GHDViPcQ6uTTfqFMqQ6KSB4f8-SHY-22InUxRf8uVjDYKqPYpc_EBjLBytMw1IbDRjo0QqWm3Qi3wzCD51oS4kRHpWfe-6zB_QcMi9VB4_y9eWGIm9yMXK1053vC6pZL3vrGMYwPUEI7TO7iHJFg47Z2dx9uaTZUmh2iCDQ98bhgK-ea4YZZKoZUmrxbUprV56ZktgqTa6_lsMUkGxBnmR_nz-_Svz7DS96vYkBwjunDV5sCHbynhUKTBWrrFH-oNVM92w61HBqNQYzbs-DFtM09YlrTqH62GaMq4W4SRSwfjOIg_SMf2C4MO69xg_Xt6wvPBrTe93zyeqLxQnRUCH77Go7almbWla5WY5r2AI-9SWPEPEeuU7gGbc-xw2WxgD6nNdg04fsAmVcyijIov12b7qpAxhZB-CrLGE6raFRyQoYLO9bat9Z300gG2LNWfOWpbTL4w2S55vzsnYJ-t6v5Ozk-zNapJJmii1PLv-IJuSJesWLjqD9Mo7KIoCntS15FF7HhykDyQPVjdw3-7GQsnjFMyZ-XP5e3I634AMfAYI6HKILxPG7f80m6dthA0FhHf3afnMeT455N5RBLksaSzp_uFuU8GVNkdNjciji1RU_kT1fBr_AXY13uVDBAAA



