```

| element | after `hydrate()` | after `mount()` |
|---|---|---|
| `h1` | `App.svelte:5:0` | `App.svelte:5:0` |
| `section` | `Card.svelte:1:0` | `Card.svelte:1:0` |
| `p` | **missing** | `App.svelte:7:0` |

**Cause.** The SSR output is `<!--[--><h1>title</h1> <section>card</section><!----> <p>after</p><!--]-->`. The component's output has no `<!--[-->`/`<!--]-->` around it, so it is at the same depth as `App`'s own elements.

When hydrating, `assign_locations` in `src/internal/client/dev/elements.js` walks siblings at depth 0 and assigns `App`'s locations in order:
1. `h1` gets `[5,0]`.
2. Card's `<section>` gets `[7,0]`, the `<p>`'s location.
3. The location list is exhausted, so `<p>` gets nothing.

Card's own `add_locations` then overwrites the `<section>`'s meta with the correct `Card.svelte:1:0`, which hides the mistake. The only visible symptom is the missing meta on `<p>`.

