### Describe the bug

Android WebView prematurely unescapes %2B into + before passing intercepted URLs across the JNI bridge, breaking Base64 query parameters that servers parse as spaces

Tauri/Wry should preserve raw encoding using uri.getEncodedQuery().

### Reproduction

1. Setup a Tauri project as usual
2. choose any frtonend app doesn't matter, i like to choose svelte with vite
3. add this svelte code
```svelte
<script>
  let status = "";

  async function sendTest(value) {
    const res = await fetch(`/test-island?e=${value}`);
    status = `${res.status}: ${await res.text()}`;
  }
</script>

<div style="height: 100px; width: 100%;"></div>

<button on:click={() => sendTest("test%2Bpayload")}>
  Test Failing Request
</button>

<button on:click={() => sendTest("testpayload")}> Test Success Request </button>

<p>{status}</p>
```
add this vite config
```ts
import { svelte } from "@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte";
import { defineConfig } from "vite";

// https://vite.dev/config/
export default defineConfig({
	plugins: [
		svelte(),

		{
			name: "mock-server-island",
			configureServer(server) {
				server.middlewares.use("/test-island", (req, res) => {
					const url = new URL(req.url || "", "http://localhost");
					const val = url.searchParams.get("e");
					if (val?.includes(" ")) {
						res.statusCode = 400;
						res.end("400 Bad Request: Base64 corrupted with space");
					} else {
						res.statusCode = 200;
						res.end("200 OK");
					}
				});
			},
		},
	],
});

```

4. setup tauri android app with `tauri androind init` as usual
5. run the tauri android dev server as usual
6. click the first button in the android device or emulator and check the request failing in the Dev tools -> Network tab with BAD request


### Expected behavior

it should not unescapes `%2B` into `+` as it doesn't behave like this on other platforms

### Full `tauri info` output

