```

### Stack trace

```text
GET http://tauri.localhost/test-island?e=test%2Bpayload 400 (Bad Request)
```

### Additional context

About how i stumbled upon this situation,
i was building an astrojs ssr app with server islands into a tauri package for android
while doing so, half of the time, my server island requests started failing
the real reason was that the server island requests also passed a encrypted base64 query paramter which 51% of the i included a `%2B` which the Android's `Uri` pipeline automatically unescape, causing it to cover from `%2B` -> `+` litteral. which the astrojs server recevies and interprets `+` as a ` ` space character. then while decrypting the base64 string with a space, it breaks the encryption

