body_text:
### Description

`InnerPath` rejects a nested route when an *outer* router capture contains invalid UTF-8, even though the capture is not part of the inner router's result.

### Reproduction

```rust
use axum::Router;
use axum::extract::InnerPath;
use axum::routing::get;

let app = Router::new().nest(
    "/org/{org}",
    Router::new().route("/team/{team_id}", get(|InnerPath(p): InnerPath<Vec<(String, String)>>| async move { p })),
);

// GET /org/%FF/team/1337
```

The outer `{org}` capture is stored as `InvalidUtf8InPathParam` before `StripPrefix` advances the inner offset. `InnerPath` then returns a 400 for `org`, even though its documented contract is to return only the captures from the innermost matched route (`team_id`).

### Expected

The invalid outer capture is ignored and the handler receives `{team_id: "1337"}`.

### Actual

The request fails with `FailedToDeserializePathParams(InvalidUtf8InPathParam { key: "org" })`.

The `InnerPath` extractor was merged in PR #3856 on 2026-09-25 and is not in the latest release. I found no existing issue or PR for this case.

