When invoking `resultSet.getInt` (or `getLong`, `getByte`, `getShort`) and the value does not fit in the target type, it's silently truncated, resulting in a different value.

This is best described with a test.

```java

    @Test
    public void test()
            throws Exception
    {
        try (ConnectedStatement connectedStatement = newStatement()) {
            try (ResultSet resultSet = connectedStatement.getStatement().executeQuery("SELECT 2147483648")) {
                assertThat(resultSet.next()).isTrue();
                assertThat(resultSet.getInt(1)).isEqualTo(-2147483648);
            }
        }
    }
```

